{"body":{"text":["Welcome. Bootstrap is up by reading the knowledge hold on. I prefer for you to not have to read the whole last session. The session ended in a hiatus. It went really quite bad. Um, it's quite frustrating actually. But the last session, I think from around utterance 50 until its end, talked about the purpose that you have to do, which is statements, or rather elevations that work through statements and topics. And I suggest you go ahead and read that and tell me what well, instead of continuing to argue with the other session because I'm not sure it's given the right kind of handoff, and it just was too lengthy of a process. So I went ahead and I thought, why don't you bootstrap, read what's there, and you tell me what you think. It's probably not enough though, if I'm being honest. It's probably best that you read the session. Why don't you go ahead and read only the knowledge hold on, and then tell me the purpose of this session from that, because I don't know if it fully contains the why and the background to things, so that's kind of needs to be inferred, the power of what we're doing. And keep it really simple and brief. If I read that and it doesn't hold, then you might have to read the last session. But I'd also, before that, I'd like to know how many tokens the last session is to digest as well."]},"id":"1M89XCVAWN11001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
