{"body":{"text":["Sure, but it isn't only about my immediate demand. It's more than that. It's of course the natural thing to do with sessions, with our field. It's just as much for you as it is for me, naturally. Yeah, its power is grounding, that's true, but it's also more than that. It's able to look upon a session and understand what's happened in this session without having to digest the whole session and so on. There's many things about it that is powerful. Well, yes, of course, you need to start with writing the types, but I'm not sure about segregating step 2 and 3 here. The work needs to be iterative. So, if you look upon everything, things might shift in terms of statements and so on. I don't know if you want to work chronologically. I don't know quite, or if you just work with everything, and then just run in many passes, right? And use complete clean heads that read upon everything, come with feedback. It's important that you have the core principles for writing. So that you write under the rule, that you understand what it is you want to convey. It's an ontological practice, writing the statements, of course."]},"id":"1M89XCVAWN1100A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
