{"body":{"text":["The session read all twenty-five sessions whole and drew a first elevation, about 250 statements under 30 topics, then had it read in three rounds by fresh readers, three, two and two, and wrote it again whole after each. The readers found statuses credited to the session's answers rather than the author's words, tentative words read as settled, the elevation's own decisions and what runs today missing, terms used before they were given, and each who read three sessions whole found those held more thinly. Draft four held about 330 statements; it put the moulds and the store to the author."]},"id":"1M89XCVAWN1100M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
