{"body":{"text":["When you say pointing at the utterance that gave it and its grounds, do you mean by grounds that is one of the status properties? Because how can a statement only point to one utterance when there can be so many? I don't get it. Did you just do a few tests here, studied? And you also give me this fucking wall of text. I can't take any wall of texts anymore. I'm sorry for my frustration, but sweet Lord. I don't see why it needs to be its own store. Oh, because the author session and the knowledge. So perhaps the sessions and the knowledge shouldn't be separated. Perhaps there should be one knowledge, one space of I don't know, this is interesting. No, it might be in separate stores, but then the it would make sense that maybe the statements and the topics reside in the same store as the knowledge, because it's not that big and the knowledge is going to be linking to it all the time. So then if you don't have the sessions, fine. Then you can still see a bit of the traces, even though you can't see them. So yeah, I think that makes sense. But I don't know. Has anything changed? You say fuck this wall of text. I mean, oh, sweet Lord, my patience is low. I'm seeing this. Has anything changed from the spec we already settled for elevation? If not, you're gonna just need to motor on here. You're going to need to read all of the sessions, but I guess you already did that because you're now at 64% used. Please write another answer. Please be... attentive to the session."]},"id":"1M89XCVAWN1100P","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
