{"body":{"text":["I don't quite get the point of by. Who's to say it's only one of the realms that the current status resides upon? But isn't it just chronological, right? Perhaps it's I don't know. I'm skeptical to that format. Let's talk about that first before I ask you to, because I don't trust that this work is done just here. I expect you to do thorough work. Maybe we leave this session and a new session gets to. It depends, because you've got quite the full context, so maybe a fresher session could be at half the context. And it's also be able to reread things and inspect them under the rule. And, it's ontology. It's breaking up the field into pieces, and that's not naturally delicate work. What do you mean done statements don't carry their commit hashes yet? Well, of course, since they're written and done first, they only have one commit. So they don't have history. That's just what it is."]},"id":"1M89XCVAWN1100T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
