{"body":{"text":["That sounds to be running ahead here to use Git commits for when the code was written like that, so on. I think it's an interesting thing to be able to look at all when something is completed and so on, but I don't know. I don't think we have, and we're not there at the moment. There's of course more such as that to do, you know. Each session naturally does work during that session. And when Git commits are integrated into the field, then 100% we should be able to correlate the commits to the session that worked on them. And if the session then has the spans over them for the statements and the topics, etc., everything will come together. So I think that's an advanced topic and we're just not there yet. So it sounds like that kind of commit hash thing is doesn't make sense to me. I guess though the commit hash regardless, even with the integration, will still make sense, but I don't know, it sounds premature. What do you mean by a short brief for the fresh session? What kind of brief? Where would you want to write that? Of course, a drop by."]},"id":"1M89XCVAWN1100Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
